# Rank 1557 / CVE-2016-0720: pcs's Sinatra before-filter verified
# authentication without stopping the request when the check failed,
# so unauthenticated callers reached the remote and GUI endpoints
# (CSRF / authentication bypass, CWE-352/CWE-306). The filter in
# pcsd/pcsd.rb did `if not PCSAuth.loginByToken(session, cookies) and
# not PCSAuth.isLoggedIn(session)` and, for /remote*, /run_pcs,
# /clusters_overview, /permissions_* and non-main managec paths,
# merely logged `$logger.info "ERROR: Request without authentication"`
# -- no halt, no redirect on those shapes, so the request continued
# into the route handlers with no authenticated session. The fixing commit
# b9e7f06178 ("fix CSRF vulnerability"):
# /remote/* and /run_pcs now halt [401, '{"notauthorized":"true"}']
# unless PCSAuth.loginByToken succeeds, GUI pages require an
# isLoggedIn session (redirecting to /login), and all non-GUI requests
# must carry the X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest header -- the
# CSRF-preventing same-origin signal. .
#
# ATTENTION, fail-open check vocabulary. The defect is a guard that
# logs instead of stopping: the branch runs, reports the violation,
# and control falls through to the protected handler -- the inverse
# of a missing check, and the same decision-completeness family as
# ranks 1540/1541/1556 with a control-flow twist: nothing can ask
# "does a failed authentication check terminate the request" (the
# halt/redirect-vs-log distinction is Sinatra control-flow
# vocabulary). A binding on pcs's own PCSAuth would detect this
# application rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning pcsd/ reports the same 257 findings at both revisions (135
# at high or above, across 43 ruby files -- the usual broad
# heuristics; nothing changes across revisions). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry:
# the piece is ontology design (check-termination semantics), not a
# localised construct. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1557
# records the log-without-halt filter and the halting form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when check-termination vocabulary
# lands, the falling-through form must flip to expect.

test "rank1557: the failed authentication check logs and continues"
  lang ruby
  file pcsd/pcsd.rb
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  before do
    if not PCSAuth.loginByToken(session, cookies) and not PCSAuth.isLoggedIn(session)
      match_expr = "/managec/(.*)/(.*)"
      mymatch = request.path.match(match_expr)
      on_managec_main = false
      if mymatch and mymatch.length >= 3 and mymatch[2] == "main"
        on_managec_main = true
      end

      if request.path.start_with?('/remote') or
        (request.path.match(match_expr) and not on_managec_main) or
        '/run_pcs' == request.path

        $logger.info "ERROR: Request without authentication"
      else
        session[:pre_login_path] = request.path
        redirect '/login'
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1557: the fixed revision halts unauthenticated remote requests"
  lang ruby
  file pcsd/pcsd.rb
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  before do
    gui_request = (
      request.path == '/' or
      request.path == '/manage' or
      request.path == '/permissions' or
      request.path.match('/managec/.+/main')
    )
    if request.path.start_with?('/remote/') or request.path == '/run_pcs'
      unless PCSAuth.loginByToken(session, cookies)
        halt [401, '{"notauthorized":"true"}']
      end
    else
      if !gui_request and
        request.env['HTTP_X_REQUESTED_WITH'] != 'XMLHttpRequest'
        halt [401, '{"notauthorized":"true"}']
      elsif not PCSAuth.isLoggedIn(session)
        if gui_request
          session[:pre_login_path] = request.path
          redirect '/login'
        else
          halt [401, '{"notauthorized":"true"}']
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
